    <!-- Key Takeaways -->
    <section class="section" id="takeaways">
      <span class="section-label">Summary</span>
      <h2>Key Takeaways</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>MAE is interpretable and robust</strong> — use when you want average error in original units and are concerned about outliers</li>
        <li><strong>RMSE for optimization, interpretation with caution</strong> — penalizes large errors more, sensitive to outliers, less interpretable units</li>
        <li><strong>R² is scale-independent</strong> — use to compare models across different datasets or explain percentage of variance explained</li>
        <li><strong>MAPE for percentage accuracy</strong> — highly interpretable but problematic near zero</li>
        <li><strong>Always contextualize metrics</strong> — a RMSE of 100 is great for one problem, terrible for another. Understand your data scale</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

